</style><header><div class="top"><h1>Lactis3</h1><div class="facts"><span><b>11</b> sessions</span><span><b>141</b> cells to fill in</span><span class="flag"><b>4</b> over one page</span></div></div><nav><a href="#antibiotic-stocks"><span class="n">1</span>Antibiotic stocks</a><a href="#oligo-dilutions"><span class="n">2</span>Oligo dilutions</a><a href="#pcr"><span class="n">3</span>PCR</a><a href="#gel-cleanup-and-assembly"><span class="n">4</span>Gel, cleanup and assembly</a><a href="#transformation"><span class="n">5</span>Transformation</a><a href="#picking"><span class="n">6</span>Picking</a><a href="#miniprep-and-sequencing"><span class="n">7</span>Miniprep and sequencing</a><a href="#sequence-analysis"><span class="n">8</span>Sequence analysis</a><a href="#electroporation"><span class="n">9</span>Electroporation</a><a href="#picking-and-inoculation"><span class="n">10</span>Picking and inoculation</a><a href="#assay"><span class="n">11</span>Assay</a><a href="#send-it-back">Send it back</a><a href="#cortex-record">cortex-record</a></nav></header><main><section id="antibiotic-stocks"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 1 · Antibiotic stocks</h2></div><p class="meta">29 rows</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Antibiotic stocks for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">protocol: preparation_of_antibiotic_1000x_stock</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: plates and media are made from these</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Preparation of erythromycin 1000× stock</td></tr><tr><td class="">100 mg/mL in ethanol.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Solvent: ETHANOL — not water. It will not dissolve in water.</td></tr><tr><td class="">1. Label a sterile 1.5 mL microcentrifuge tube.</td></tr><tr><td class="">2. Place the empty tube on an analytical balance and tare to 0.000 g.</td></tr><tr><td class="">3. Scoop approximately 50 mg of antibiotic powder into the tube; record the actual mass (mg).</td></tr><tr><td class="">4. Compute the volume of solvent for a 100 mg/mL stock by multiplying the mass you recorded by 10 — that is, volume (µL) = mass (mg) × 10. Add that volume of ethanol. (Worked example: 50 mg × 10 = 500 µL (0.50 mL). Use your own recorded mass, not this number.)</td></tr><tr><td class="">5. Cap the tube and vortex until fully dissolved; avoid aerosols. It is slow, so be patient. In hot agar it clouds briefly and clears on swirling.</td></tr><tr><td class="">6. If a sterile stock is required, sterile‑filter (0.22 µm) into a sterile, labeled tube using a membrane compatible with the solvent.</td></tr><tr><td class="">7. Aliquot as needed and label with antibiotic, concentration, date, and your initials.</td></tr><tr><td class="">8. Store according to lab SOP for this antibiotic (commonly −20 °C or 4 °C).</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">The inventory does not record a stock of erm. Check the shelf before you weigh anything — if there is one, write down where you found it and skip this session.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Plates and media are made from this stock, so it comes before everything else.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="oligo-dilutions"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 2 · Oligo dilutions</h2></div><p class="meta">34 rows</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Oligo dilutions for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: 100 uM stocks down to the 10 uM the PCR uses</td></tr><tr><td class="b">1. Find the 100 uM stocks</td></tr><tr><td class="">These already exist. Write down the box and well you actually took each one from — that is how the inventory learns where they are, and the next person does not repeat this search.</td></tr><tr><td class="h">oligo</td><td class="h">what it is for</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf029</td><td class="">PCR primer for pBET8</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf030</td><td class="">PCR primer for pBET8</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf027</td><td class="">PCR primer for pBET8</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf028</td><td class="">PCR primer for pBET8</td></tr><tr><td class="b">2. Make the 10 uM working stocks</td></tr><tr><td class="">These are what the PCR actually uses. Nothing to work out — the volumes below make 100 uL of 10 uM from the 100 uM stock.</td></tr><tr><td class="h">oligo</td><td class="h">uL of 100 uM stock</td><td class="h">uL ddH2O</td><td class="h">final volume</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf029</td><td class="">10</td><td class="">90</td><td class="">100</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf030</td><td class="">10</td><td class="">90</td><td class="">100</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf027</td><td class="">10</td><td class="">90</td><td class="">100</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf028</td><td class="">10</td><td class="">90</td><td class="">100</td></tr><tr><td class="">Label every tube with the oligo name and the concentration. A 100 uM tube and a 10 uM tube look identical.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">The inventory does not record where bf029, bf030, bf027, bf028 live. That is a gap in the document, not proof they are missing — write down where you find them and the inventory is updated from this sheet when it comes back.</td></tr><tr><td class="">STILL TO DECIDE: where the 4 unlocated oligo stock(s) are — the sheet asks, and the returned workbook is what updates the inventory</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="pcr"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 3 · PCR</h2></div><p class="meta">42 rows</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">PCR for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">protocol: primestar_pcr</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: PCR is a day. Running that is long.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">When you are done</td><td class="">put the tubes in the to-gel box</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Source</td></tr><tr><td class="h">what</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td><td class="h">note</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf029</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E18=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E18)</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F18=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F18)</td><td class="">the 10 µM working stock you made in session 2</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf030</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E19=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E19)</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F19=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F19)</td><td class="">the 10 µM working stock you made in session 2</td></tr><tr><td class="b">pJ01</td><td class="">Pink Training</td><td class="n"></td><td class="">Miniprep DNA in Pink Training. Also in Control Stocks.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf027</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E20=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E20)</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F20=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F20)</td><td class="">the 10 µM working stock you made in session 2</td></tr><tr><td class="b">bf028</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E21=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!E21)</td><td class="f">=IF(&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F21=&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;,&#x27;Oligo dilutions&#x27;!F21)</td><td class="">the 10 µM working stock you made in session 2</td></tr><tr><td class="b">pTRKH3-slpGFP</td><td class="">Control Stocks</td><td class="n"></td><td class="">Miniprep DNA in Control Stocks.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Samples</td></tr><tr><td class="h">label</td><td class="h">construct</td><td class="h">forward oligo</td><td class="h">reverse oligo</td><td class="h">template</td><td class="h">expected size</td><td class="h">program</td></tr><tr><td class="">L3a</td><td class="">Pcon-amilGFP-Term</td><td class="">bf029</td><td class="">bf030</td><td class="">pJ01</td><td class="">1384 bp</td><td class="">PG2K55</td></tr><tr><td class="">L3b</td><td class="">backbone</td><td class="">bf027</td><td class="">bf028</td><td class="">pTRKH3-slpGFP</td><td class="">6559 bp</td><td class="">PG8K55</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Reaction</td></tr><tr><td class="">2 samples — set the reaction up directly. A mastermix is worth it from 4.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">32 uL</td><td class="">ddH2O (white)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">10 uL</td><td class="">5X PrimeSTAR GXL Buffer (green)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">4 uL</td><td class="">PrimeSTAR dNTP Mixture (2.5 mM each, yellow)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">1 uL</td><td class="">10 uM primer 1 (white)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">1 uL</td><td class="">10 uM primer 2 (white)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">1 uL</td><td class="">dil20x plasmid template (white)</td></tr><tr><td class="b">1 uL</td><td class="">PrimeSTAR GXL DNA Polymerase</td></tr><tr><td class="b">PrimeSTAR GXL PCR — use the pcr cheatsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="">Set up 2 × 50 µL PCRs — the primer pair and template for each are in the Samples table above.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="gel-cleanup-and-assembly"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 4 · Gel, cleanup and assembly</h2></div><p class="meta">50 rows · <span class="flag">over one printed page (6 rows too many)</span></p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Gel, cleanup and assembly for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">protocol: analytical_gel</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: one sitting, but a long one — and a long labsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Source</td></tr><tr><td class="h">what</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td><td class="h">note</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Pcon-amilGFP-Term</td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="">made by the pcr step that produces Pcon-amilGFP-Term</td></tr><tr><td class="b">backbone</td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="">made by the pcr step that produces backbone</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Samples</td></tr><tr><td class="h">loads tube</td><td class="h">construct</td><td class="h">expected size</td></tr><tr><td class="">L3a</td><td class="">Pcon-amilGFP-Term</td><td class="">1384 bp</td></tr><tr><td class="">L3b</td><td class="">backbone</td><td class="">6559 bp</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Analytical Gel — use the gel cheatsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="">Run 2 samples plus a marker on a 1% analytical agarose gel.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Cleanup</td></tr><tr><td class="h">label</td><td class="h">from</td><td class="h">construct</td><td class="h">size</td></tr><tr><td class="">zL3a</td><td class="">L3a</td><td class="">Pcon-amilGFP-Term</td><td class="">1384 bp</td></tr><tr><td class="">zL3b</td><td class="">L3b</td><td class="">backbone</td><td class="">6559 bp</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Zymo Cleanup — use the zymo cheatsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="">Clean 2 reactions on a Zymo column, eluting in 25 µL.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Golden Gate assembly</td></tr><tr><td class="h">label</td><td class="h">construct</td><td class="h">fragments</td><td class="h">enzyme</td></tr><tr><td class="">L3c</td><td class="">gg</td><td class="">zL3a  +  zL3b</td><td 