/td></tr><tr><td class="">Photograph the plates under blue and ambient before picking. The photographs are the record of what you chose between.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">CHECKPOINT</td><td class="">send this in before carrying on</td></tr><tr><td class="h">What to send</td><td class="">a photo of each plate before you picked, under every lighting the sheet names, and the colony counts</td></tr><tr><td class="h">Email it to</td><td class="">jca-cortex@berkeley.edu</td></tr><tr><td class="h">Put this line in the message</td><td class="e">cortex::lactis3_s6_pick</td></tr><tr><td class="">That line is how the lab&#x27;s system knows which experiment and which step your message belongs to. Copy it exactly.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="miniprep-and-sequencing"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 7 · Miniprep and sequencing</h2></div><p class="meta">40 rows</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Miniprep and sequencing for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">protocol: qiagen_miniprep</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: together — the submission follows straight off the prep</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Source</td></tr><tr><td class="h">what</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td><td class="h">note</td></tr><tr><td class="b">JTK165-AB/pBET8-A</td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="">made by the pick step that produces JTK165-AB/pBET8-A</td></tr><tr><td class="b">JTK165-AB/pBET8-B</td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="">made by the pick step that produces JTK165-AB/pBET8-B</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Samples</td></tr><tr><td class="h">label</td><td class="h">from block</td><td class="h">Box</td><td class="h">Well</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-A</td><td class="">L3e</td><td class="">cheese_temp</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-B</td><td class="">L3f</td><td class="">cheese_temp</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Qiagen Miniprep — use the miniprep cheatsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="">Purify plasmid DNA from a saturated culture by alkaline lysis and spin column.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Sequencing</td></tr><tr><td class="h">label</td><td class="h">template</td><td class="h">oligo</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-AF</td><td class="">pBET8-A</td><td class="">bf037</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-AR</td><td class="">pBET8-A</td><td class="">bf038</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-BF</td><td class="">pBET8-B</td><td class="">bf037</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-BR</td><td class="">pBET8-B</td><td class="">bf038</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Cycle Sequencing — use the sequencing cheatsheet</td></tr><tr><td class="">Submit 4 reads with primer G00101 on dGTP chemistry.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Write the name on the cap AND on the side of the tube. A cap in a freezer box is read from above and a tube in your hand is read from the side, and a box of unlabelled sides is a box you have to open tube by tube.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Write the well for every tube before it goes in the freezer. These rows are what the inventory is updated from when the workbook comes back.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="sequence-analysis"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 8 · Sequence analysis</h2></div><p class="meta">45 rows · <span class="flag">over one printed page (1 rows too many)</span></p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Sequence analysis for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: desk work, no bench</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Samples</td></tr><tr><td class="h">clone</td><td class="h">reads</td><td class="h">result</td><td class="h">explanation</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-A</td><td class="">pBET8-AF, pBET8-AR</td></tr><tr><td class="">pBET8-B</td><td class="">pBET8-BF, pBET8-BR</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Result tokens — use one of these exactly</td></tr><tr><td class="h">token</td><td class="h">what it means</td></tr><tr><td class="">Perfect</td><td class="">Full region covered, matches the model.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Perfect Partial</td><td class="">Matches where readable, but the region is not fully covered.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Silent Mutation</td><td class="">Base change in the ORF, same amino acid.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Missense Mutation</td><td class="">Base change in the ORF, the amino acid changes.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Nonsense Mutation</td><td class="">Base change in the ORF, creates a stop codon.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Indel</td><td class="">Insertion or deletion in the region — may frameshift.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Mixed Clone</td><td class="">Two sequences in one trace; the colony was not clonal.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Failed</td><td class="">Read unusable, or it will not align to the target.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">The single clone you are most confident about</td></tr><tr><td class="h">clone</td><td class="h">why</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Align every read against the intended sequence of the construct, not against each other.</td></tr><tr><td class="">The whole confirmation region may not be readable. Pay attention to the assembly junctions and to consistency with the model.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Throw out any miniprep that is not Perfect or Perfect Partial. A tube nobody trusts that stays in the box is a tube somebody uses next year.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Write down which clone passed. Every session after this one fetches that tube, and if the answer is not on this sheet it