pBET8</td><td class="">pBET8</td><td class="">L.lactis</td><td class="">Erm</td><td class="">30</td><td class="">electroporation</td></tr><tr><td class="b">For this experiment</td></tr><tr><td class="b">negative</td><td class="">untransformed</td></tr><tr><td class="b">positive</td><td class="">pTRKH3-slpGFP</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">3 plates: the sample, plus untransformed (negative) and pTRKH3-slpGFP (positive). Every plate is electroporated the same way.</td></tr><tr><td class="">No electroporation protocol is in the library yet, so this sheet carries the conditions and not the procedure. Nothing here tells you the cuvette gap, the voltage or the recovery medium.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">CHECKPOINT</td><td class="">send this in before carrying on</td></tr><tr><td class="h">What to send</td><td class="">a photo of every plate including both controls, and the colony counts</td></tr><tr><td class="h">Email it to</td><td class="">jca-cortex@berkeley.edu</td></tr><tr><td class="h">Put this line in the message</td><td class="e">cortex::lactis3_s9_retransform</td></tr><tr><td class="">That line is how the lab&#x27;s system knows which experiment and which step your message belongs to. Copy it exactly.</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your notes</td></tr><tr><td class="">Anything that happened that the plan did not say. This comes back with the file and becomes part of the record.</td></tr></table></div></section><section id="picking-and-inoculation"><div class="sh"><h2>Session 10 · Picking and inoculation</h2></div><p class="meta">47 rows · <span class="flag">over one printed page (3 rows too many)</span></p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><td class="b">Picking and inoculation for Experiment Lactis3</td></tr><tr><td class="b">Your name</td><td class="e"></td><td class="n"></td><td class="b">Date</td></tr><tr><td class="">protocol: picking_colonies_into_block</td></tr><tr><td class="">source: of the retransformation; the block is inoculated as